title: 'The GUI fixture preview harness ships: a design-fidelity loop with no kernel'
summary: '2777cf60 (plus 96191003, which fixed the symbols-drift failure from the WIP commits). `node packages/gnomon-gui/scripts/preview.mjs` renders the real GUI over a fake kernel transport, so the real auth and serverSig path runs. The cards are signed with a per-page throwaway key so their buttons render. Six fixtures, each in day and night with motion on or off: desk, empty, voice-armed, voice-crashed, stack-heavy and workshop. Workshop runs the real mod model. preview-shots.mjs --chrome writes all 12 PNGs in about 7 s using headless Chrome, with no new dependency. The preview code is proven absent from the pinned bundle, and the G-WEB-08 hash is unchanged. Baseline shots taken. The desk shows the remaining gaps: a ''Georgia'' title font, no activity folding, hsid names, markdown rendered raw (**bold**), a flat stack, and no Workshop slot.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#gui'
  - '#gui-preview'
learnings:
  - A fake transport behind the real client exercises the real auth path and makes visual QA cheap; build it before any UI restyle.
